{
 "header": {
  "apiLevel": 7,
  "width": 420,
  "height": 420,
  "profiles": 513,
  "contentDescription": "An IKEA MICKE desk assembling itself in 3D as a white line drawing: every panel filled in pale grey and outlined in black, like a technical illustration. Cabinet, shelves, steel leg, modesty panel, top, door and drawer each fly into place in the order the manual builds them. Drag to turn it."
 },
 "//": [
  "MICKE desk (105x50), from assembly manual AA-476615-12.",
  "",
  "Dimensions are METRES and are the real ones. The origin is the floor at the",
  "centre of the desk: +y up, +x along the width, +z toward the viewer.",
  "",
  "Each part flies in during its own window of a 26 second cycle. To change the",
  "order, reorder PARTS in tools/mk_ikea_desk.py - the timing is derived from a",
  "part's index, not written down per part.",
  "",
  "Drag to turn the desk; it coasts to a stop when you let go."
 ],
